86045417] [17592186113917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186492423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186492497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186492510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186492582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113917 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113917 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113917 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186492497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113917 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6c202514-58b0-57fd-9d4a-d9d9f27c390e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113918 #edb/ref 1080 "No solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113918 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113918 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "90d6f3fc-4b07-573d-909e-71ad76038bc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113923 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113923 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113923 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113923 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e3a07998-8f4c-5e30-bdee-b2acbf389fbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115070 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4711" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115070 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](images/40/406033f059dc4438ea55d43d2bd00b3b79bb99365a2e4846c995f4a447acfd82.svg)\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115070 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dc6dd9b4-de7f-52d0-8ff9-a7a7f7a9abd7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115070 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](images/be/bed2784d17ee63b805917b492052daa7ef079c1682bbc78468eb10f314a92b1f.svg)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/91/91175ab97472067cd14ffff740bb3a98718436f1e94de7a4a6d7fdfb1b35b81f.svg)\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1-5y \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115071 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4712" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115071 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y &=1, \\\\ 4x+ky &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115071 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f2c7cfd3-da43-5208-bd0e-21692357fabe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115071 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](images/6f/6fa4508463b059ce8ef9a5cfa720de9463e41ecdbfb16f4460870bb6fce444bc.svg)\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n![](images/21/215ff061dc7584055bf607f48d0048cb6bde4dcb1ed028fbf4c3a4bd47d89c25.svg)\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115124 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6173" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115124 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system\n![](images/0e/0e89fc57b6af2ddf2a71246dbadc7feb8425d1e1e0ab8f988e7e8ad97d22cff7.svg)\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n\n- The system has no solution\n\n- The system is consistent independent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115124 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cd56314d-f45a-55be-9762-983fe507a1a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115124 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](images/3e/3e3e8adb0d6e13f7d3b4c3e450b25a789480ac53189ab92385174688e460b2cc.svg)\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/41/4122fb4ef56aa99161b15bc25001ca728a6cf7dae36d5dac0aac9b03dc411685.svg)\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186402009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186402756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186417081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557520 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557532 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557536 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557548 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557549 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557551 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557557 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557558 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115241 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557567 #edb/r