edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186300447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9bc72922-bebc-50a1-a8ff-483d8fbfcfc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32245" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=3 \\\\ 4x+ky &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "534e2a93-e71a-5475-894e-dfd5ca99a3a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & k & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & k & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & k+2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=3 \\\\ (k+2)y &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nNow if $k=-2$, then the second equation is $0=-2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when  $k=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186302143 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302143 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32331" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302143 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302143 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-y &=2 \\\\ 8x+ky &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186302143 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f5f8dda9-f72e-566e-91bc-44ecdce08b8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302143 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & k & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & k & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-y &=2 \\\\ (k-2)y &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=2,$ then the second equation is $0=9,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186343154 #edb/ref 1080 "k=5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343154 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343154 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6b9a3770-af37-58af-91e7-3430fd2463b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343221 #edb/ref 1080 "k=3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343221 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343221 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "71cae964-c567-5585-ab23-7241fb114732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343724 #edb/ref 1080 "k=1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343724 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343724 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a8f3da90-4b17-5b45-af78-2746f79a0b95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343764 #edb/ref 1080 "k=9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343764 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343764 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ad97781e-f202-56a0-803a-f17ee1a49ca9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344356 #edb/ref 1080 "k=7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344356 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344356 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f0d5b11f-4138-5c57-8bc8-f9f3a404cfaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186344356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6517af05-6089-578f-972a-9310f8010c94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363108 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186438965 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186363108 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186438966 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186363108 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186438967 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186363108 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131718" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363108 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363108 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=2 \\\\ -2x+7y+2z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186363108 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8de2435-5f56-5017-bf79-0b535c719854" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363108 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+2z &=2 \\\\ y-z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "013e11bb-39c0-595b-a244-03847638286f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=0 \\\\ y-z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=0 \\\\ y &=z-1 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186402761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0fa49e40-cb09-52a9-be51-216ec3f67938" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402758 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186402758 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402758 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e80e6ba-d53c-56a1-8f14-814656e252d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402759 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186402759 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402759 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "240d49db-221f-5c96-a2c7-752016dd8d06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402760 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-z \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186402760 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402760 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c205ae90-dae6-5981-8476-c566174adf7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402761 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186402761 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402761 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a7eb10d8-4da4-5dab-bc8c-4a003f7cebfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402762 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186402762 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402762 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c70e171e-d942-5f58-90b7-b6fb6a232836" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402763 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186439174 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186402763 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186439175 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186402763 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186439176 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186402763 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42020" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402763 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402763 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 3x+y &=3 \\\\ -2x+y &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system has a unique solution\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186402763 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a930b2a-2578-5145-8e40-06b6cab16ba9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402763 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=2,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186425937 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425937 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425937 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425937 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425937 #edb/ref 1045 "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425937 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186425950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425937 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425937 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425937 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "080f971c-621c-5ccf-b883-b98c49745b79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425938 #edb/ref 1080 "k=1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425938 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425938 #edb/